## 3. Design System

### Typography (two families, proposal pending client confirmation)
The PDF embeds **Caladea** (serif) and **Carlito** (sans), which are metric-compatible stand-ins for Cambria and Calibri. The brand fonts are therefore unconfirmed.
- **Display:** `Caladea`, tight-to-moderate tracking, uppercase for section headlines.
- **Body and UI:** `Lato` (Carlito is derived from Lato), 16–18px, line-height 1.6.
- **Headline pattern (from the catalogue):** two weights in one line, with the first word(s) light and muted and the key word(s) bold, for example `ABOUT` **`FAB HAUS`**.
- **Labels:** small uppercase, very wide letter-spacing (`text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.25em]`), body family.
- Fluid headline size with `clamp`, up to about 120px on 1440px desktop. Check that long uppercase titles do not overflow at 360px.
- Project metadata is unboxed text separated by `·` or `/`. No pill badges, except the four specification chips in Materials & Specifications, which come from the catalogue.
- The wordmark is flat gold. The catalogue's glowing metallic effect is not reproduced.

### Color tokens
Sampled from the catalogue PDF. Hex values are approximate and must be confirmed by the client. Held in CSS variables so they can be swapped in one place.

| Token | Value (sampled) | Use |
| :-- | :-- | :-- |
| `--color-bg` | `#0E0E0E` | Page canvas, dark sections |
| `--color-surface` | `#1E1B1B` | Cards and alternate dark sections |
| `--color-text` | `#F4EBDD` | Primary text on dark |
| `--color-muted` | `#A3A3A3` | Secondary text (not from the catalogue, kept from the earlier proposal) |
| `--color-accent` | `#B8975A` (gold) | Labels, numerals and active states **on dark backgrounds only** |
| `--color-brand` | `#9E1B24` (red) | Primary buttons, stat blocks, labels on light backgrounds, table header |
| `--color-light` | `#F4EBDD` (cream) | Light-section background |
| `--color-sand` | `#E3D5BD` | Image-fallback blocks, table label column, light cards |

Rules:
- Two accents, each with a fixed job: gold on dark, red on light.
- **Never set gold text on cream or sand.** It measures about 2.3:1 and fails WCAG AA. Gold on `#0E0E0E` is about 7:1 and red on cream is about 6.7:1, both fine.
- No gradients except a dark overlay for text legibility over photos. Hairline borders at 8–12% opacity.

### Layout
- 12-column grid, 120px+ vertical rhythm between sections on desktop (80px on mobile).
- The hero slider is full-bleed. All other sections use a centered container (max-width 1280px, 20px padding on mobile) on full-width background bands alternating `--color-bg`, `--color-surface` and `--color-light`.
- Cards (segments, process steps, testimonials) are allowed: `--color-surface` background, hairline border, no shadows.
- Hero height is `min(100svh, 900px)`. Use `svh`, never `vh`, so mobile browser bars do not clip content.

