## 5. Motion System

Motion follows the simple, component-driven style of the reference site: a slider, a compare slider, a carousel and gentle reveals. There is no scroll-linked motion.

### Principles
- Calm and simple. No bounce, no spring overshoot, no flashy effects.
- Animate only `transform` and `opacity`. Never animate width, height, top or left.
- Motion never hides content: everything is readable without it.
- Not used in this layout: parallax, pinned sections, masked line reveals, clip-path wipes, count-ups, smooth-scroll libraries.

### Tokens

| Token | Value |
| :-- | :-- |
| Ease (reveals, UI) | `cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)` |
| Slide crossfade | 1.0s |
| Slide zoom (Ken Burns) | `scale 1 → 1.06` over the slide's visible time |
| Autoplay interval (hero) | 6s per slide |
| Duration, text reveal | 0.6s |
| Duration, image reveal | 0.8s |
| Duration, small UI | 0.3s |
| Stagger, cards or columns | 0.1s |
| Reveal trigger | element top at 85% of the viewport, play once (IntersectionObserver) |

### Behaviour by component

**Hero slider**
- Crossfade between slides (`opacity`), with a slow zoom on the active slide's image.
- On each slide change, the label, headline, tagline and button fade and rise in sequence (`opacity 0 → 1`, `y 24 → 0`, 0.1s apart).
- Autoplay every 6s. Autoplay stops on hover, on keyboard focus inside the slider, when the browser tab is hidden, when the pause button is pressed, and when reduced motion is on.
- Swipe on touch, arrow keys when focused, dots and arrows both clickable.
- Only the first slide's image is preloaded. Autoplay starts after the first slide has loaded.

**Header**
- Sticky. Transparent to solid background change after 80px of scroll (`opacity` of the background layer, 0.3s). The utility bar scrolls away.
- Dropdown opens on hover or focus (desktop) and on tap (touch) with a 0.2s fade and 8px rise. It is keyboard operable (`Enter`/`Space` opens, `Esc` closes).

**Section reveals**
- Headings, text, buttons and cards fade and rise once on entry. Cards and columns stagger by 0.1s.
- Images fade in with a slight settle (`opacity 0 → 1`, `scale 1.04 → 1`, 0.8s).
- Initial hidden states are applied by JavaScript after mount (`html.js` class), never by plain CSS, so content is not invisible if JS fails to load.

**Render vs Reality (compare slider)**
- Starts at 50%. The visitor drags the handle (pointer events), or uses the left/right arrow keys when it is focused.
- The top image is revealed by a clip applied to it. The handle moves with `transform`.
- Exposed as `role="slider"` with `aria-valuemin`, `aria-valuemax`, `aria-valuenow` and an accessible name.

**Segment, project and other cards**
- No scroll-linked motion. Hover (fine pointer only): image zooms `1 → 1.03` over 0.5s, link underline draws in, `↗` arrow nudges 4px.

**Testimonials carousel**
- Slides horizontally (0.5s). Arrows and swipe. Autoplay is off by default.

**Floating action buttons**
- Fade in 0.3s after load. No other motion.

**New catalogue sections** (Four Disciplines, Prefab & LGSF, tables, FH_Modulars, Signature Projects, Process)
- Use the standard section reveal only: heading, text and cards fade and rise once, cards stagger by 0.1s, images settle in.
- Tables reveal as one block. Rows do not animate individually.
- Process: the connecting line is static. Steps stagger in on entry, with no draw-on animation.
- The `3x to 4x` figure and all stats are static. No count-ups.
- Specification chips are static.
- Signature Project cards follow the card hover rule above (image zoom on fine pointers only).

### Anchors and scrolling
- Native browser scrolling everywhere. In-page anchors use CSS `scroll-behavior: smooth` (switched off under reduced motion) and `scroll-margin-top` equal to the header height.

### Hover and micro-interactions (devices with hover and a fine pointer only)
- Buttons: fill slides in from the left (0.3s), arrow nudges 4px.
- Nav links: underline draws from the left.
- All hover-revealed information is **always visible on touch devices**.

